did you know that one in five teenagers  has a serious mental illness or the  mental illness has been linked to  substance abuse and suicide and  teenagers mental health disorders like  depression and anxiety are among the  most serious problems facing our society  today in order for us to better diagnose  and treat mental illness we first must  understand what it looks like in the  brain and that's what we're setting up  to do we are the Boston adolescent  neuroimaging of depression and anxiety  consortium or abanda for short banda  uses non-invasive state-of-the-art brain  imaging to identify brain markers of  anxiety and depression and teenagers  right now it takes an average of nine  years before teenagers start treatment  for mental illness at Vanda we believe  that these brain markers will help us  identify teens at risk for anxiety and  depression much sooner and hopefully  improve the way we treat mental illness  all together to learn more or to join  our team brain project visit us at banda  MIT edu
 

